00:21:07.800 --> 00:21:09.920
So now, we can talk
about App Engine.

00:21:09.920 --> 00:21:13.010
App Engine is Google's fully
managed serverless platform

00:21:13.010 --> 00:21:15.080
as a service product
that allows you to build

00:21:15.080 --> 00:21:17.390
highly scalable applications.

00:21:17.390 --> 00:21:20.510
The underlying infrastructure
is taking care of for you.

00:21:20.510 --> 00:21:22.730
With support for multiple
programming languages,

00:21:22.730 --> 00:21:25.100
App Engine enables
developers to focus

00:21:25.100 --> 00:21:27.740
on developing their applications
without needing to worry

00:21:27.740 --> 00:21:31.310
about infrastructure concerns.

00:21:31.310 --> 00:21:33.410
You can deploy your
webhook to App Engine

00:21:33.410 --> 00:21:36.350
by running the gcloud
app deploy command.

00:21:36.350 --> 00:21:40.400
App Engine will find your
app.yaml file for your service,

00:21:40.400 --> 00:21:42.470
read any additional
parameters that you

00:21:42.470 --> 00:21:46.010
set, such as version number
runtime and service name,

00:21:46.010 --> 00:21:48.110
and deploy your application.

00:21:48.110 --> 00:21:51.320
To run your app locally before
pushing it to production,

00:21:51.320 --> 00:21:54.950
you can run the dev_appserver.py
command, for example,

00:21:54.950 --> 00:21:57.025
to test your Python
app from Cloud Shell.

00:21:59.950 --> 00:22:03.130
So in our HR chatbot
example, the webhook

00:22:03.130 --> 00:22:06.370
is called by the Dialogflow
agent's fulfillment component

00:22:06.370 --> 00:22:10.510
to get answers from Datastore
once a topic entity is matched.

00:22:10.510 --> 00:22:12.520
The webhook code
uses information

00:22:12.520 --> 00:22:16.330
from the HTTP post
request sent by your agent

00:22:16.330 --> 00:22:18.970
to look up the keyword and
match it with the topic

00:22:18.970 --> 00:22:21.190
entity in Cloud Datastore.

00:22:21.190 --> 00:22:23.290
The webhook will then
return a response

00:22:23.290 --> 00:22:26.400
back to the user, which contains
the definition of the keyword

00:22:26.400 --> 00:22:28.370
passed in the request.

