00:28:47.850 --> 00:28:50.640
So a quick recap of some
things we just did--

00:28:50.640 --> 00:28:52.890
we added HTTP basic
authentication

00:28:52.890 --> 00:28:55.620
to our webhook to prevent
unauthorized access.

00:28:55.620 --> 00:28:57.840
And so this ensures that
unauthorized callers

00:28:57.840 --> 00:28:59.570
can't call our webhook.

00:28:59.570 --> 00:29:01.800
And in the webhook
code, we implemented

00:29:01.800 --> 00:29:06.130
flask security framework for
a HTTP basic authentication.

00:29:06.130 --> 00:29:08.340
So this requires_auth
method requires

00:29:08.340 --> 00:29:11.130
authentication to
access our app.

00:29:11.130 --> 00:29:14.700
And we had a check_auth method
which validates the submitted

00:29:14.700 --> 00:29:16.480
user name and password.

00:29:16.480 --> 00:29:20.190
So these user name and password
values in this code snippet

00:29:20.190 --> 00:29:23.700
are what we used in
the Dialogflow console.

00:29:23.700 --> 00:29:27.150
And then the authenticate
method sends a 401 response

00:29:27.150 --> 00:29:28.890
if authentication fails.

00:29:28.890 --> 00:29:32.790
And so we also had to add
this requires_auth decorator

00:29:32.790 --> 00:29:35.910
to our handle method to ensure
that the method validates

00:29:35.910 --> 00:29:39.930
those authorization credentials.

00:29:39.930 --> 00:29:42.840
So besides having a
