00:30:29.400 --> 00:30:33.150
to Google Home devices,
these all rely on the actions

00:30:33.150 --> 00:30:36.880
SDK for creating the actions
that form your agent.

00:30:36.880 --> 00:30:39.390
This allows you to seamlessly
move between surfaces

00:30:39.390 --> 00:30:42.660
for the same agent no matter
which platform or functionality

00:30:42.660 --> 00:30:45.330
you need.

00:30:45.330 --> 00:30:47.730
So a quick recap of our
course and some things

00:30:47.730 --> 00:30:49.500
that we just previewed--

00:30:49.500 --> 00:30:51.337
conversation is the new UI.

00:30:51.337 --> 00:30:52.920
And it's very quickly
changing the way

00:30:52.920 --> 00:30:55.440
that users communicate
with businesses, employers,

00:30:55.440 --> 00:30:56.202
and others.

00:30:56.202 --> 00:30:57.660
We looked at some
of the challenges

00:30:57.660 --> 00:30:59.610
when creating
conversational agents that

00:30:59.610 --> 00:31:01.290
can handle natural
language input

00:31:01.290 --> 00:31:04.530
and discussed how Dialogflow can
address some of these concerns.

00:31:04.530 --> 00:31:06.369
And through the life
of a conversation,

00:31:06.369 --> 00:31:08.160
we looked at some of
the essential elements

00:31:08.160 --> 00:31:09.630
that you want your
chatbot to have,

00:31:09.630 --> 00:31:13.530
like intents, entities,
context, and fulfillment.

00:31:13.530 --> 00:31:15.900
You also learned how to
define intents and entities

00:31:15.900 --> 00:31:18.120
using the Dialogflow UI.

00:31:18.120 --> 00:31:20.130
And in the HR
chatbot example, we

00:31:20.130 --> 00:31:23.010
leveraged an existing data
source to extract entities

00:31:23.010 --> 00:31:26.250
from your Dialogflow agent.

00:31:26.250 --> 00:31:29.310
And we learned that being
able to maintain context

00:31:29.310 --> 00:31:32.100
is important for the agent to
be able to control the flow

00:31:32.100 --> 00:31:35.600
and minimize repetition and
improve overall satisfaction.

00:31:35.600 --> 00:31:37.620
And with fulfillment, you
can add functionality,

00:31:37.620 --> 00:31:41.490
like connecting to
back end systems.

00:31:41.490 --> 00:31:44.430
We then saw the coming
together of GCP products

00:31:44.430 --> 00:31:46.890
to productionize your agent,
like deploying your webhook

00:31:46.890 --> 00:31:49.710
on App Engine so it can
scale, building a knowledge

00:31:49.710 --> 00:31:52.890
base in Cloud Datastore by
leveraging the HR manual,

00:31:52.890 --> 00:31:56.160
and using the Natural Language
API to generate synonyms

00:31:56.160 --> 00:31:57.900
and adding security.

00:31:57.900 --> 00:32:01.170
And then towards the end, we
talked about how you can easily

00:32:01.170 --> 00:32:03.150
integrate your agent
into other surfaces,

00:32:03.150 --> 00:32:06.232
like the Google Assistant, and
demonstrated some of the newer

00:32:06.232 --> 00:32:07.065
additional features.

