00:34:34.280 --> 00:34:36.340
So we are back
with some questions

00:34:36.340 --> 00:34:39.580
from the audience for
Dialogflow and everything

00:34:39.580 --> 00:34:41.270
that we just talked about.

00:34:41.270 --> 00:34:43.570
So let's look at
the first question.

00:34:43.570 --> 00:34:46.810
We use .NET or any other
development platform.

00:34:46.810 --> 00:34:49.780
Can I use Dialogflow
from our environment?

00:34:49.780 --> 00:34:51.969
So the answer to
that one is yes.

00:34:51.969 --> 00:34:55.600
So the example that I showed
and that we talk about

00:34:55.600 --> 00:34:58.270
in the Coursera course
is all using Python,

00:34:58.270 --> 00:35:01.370
but that is definitely
not the only option.

00:35:01.370 --> 00:35:04.330
There are a ton of different
Dialogflow fulfillment

00:35:04.330 --> 00:35:05.680
libraries that are available.

00:35:05.680 --> 00:35:07.600
And a lot of them
are already written

00:35:07.600 --> 00:35:10.930
and ready to use on
Dialogflow's GitHub page.

00:35:10.930 --> 00:35:18.490
So we have .NET, Node.js,
Java, Python, C#, and Ruby.

00:35:18.490 --> 00:35:20.230
I think those are the ones.

00:35:20.230 --> 00:35:22.150
I don't believe
I've left any out.

00:35:22.150 --> 00:35:23.830
But the answer is
yes, definitely.

00:35:23.830 --> 00:35:25.390
And then, of course,
another option

00:35:25.390 --> 00:35:29.950
would also be just to use
the REST API calls to use

00:35:29.950 --> 00:35:33.170
the Dialogflow interface.

00:35:33.170 --> 00:35:33.670
OK.

00:35:33.670 --> 00:35:37.510
So second question, we have
developed our own specialized

00:35:37.510 --> 00:35:40.870
speech to text or use
another third party's.

00:35:40.870 --> 00:35:43.210
Can I use it with Dialogflow?

00:35:43.210 --> 00:35:45.730
So the answer to
that one is also yes.

00:35:45.730 --> 00:35:48.880
Because of that REST
API integration,

00:35:48.880 --> 00:35:51.580
you can integrate
your own speech

00:35:51.580 --> 00:35:55.060
to text API with Dialogflow
speech to text API.

00:35:55.060 --> 00:35:57.340
So that would definitely work.

